-- A visit is at most 600 minutes, and a deposit request is at least 10 and at most 1000, so 600,
-- 10, and 1000 are allowed. `velle compare` from an empty spec (an empty file) to this file
-- prints, under "The spec as a whole", this line, followed in the report by its "In the spec:"
-- lines, left out here:
--
--   - The compiler now writes 7 more example tests from the spec. They check that a new MakeDeposit produces a Deposit, by RecordDeposit, that a MakeDeposit whose amount is above 1000 is refused, that a MakeDeposit whose amount is below 10 is refused, that a MakeDeposit whose amount is 10 is accepted, that a MakeDeposit whose amount is 999 is accepted, that a Visit whose minutes is above 600 is refused, and that a Visit whose minutes is 599 is accepted.
--
-- Under `<` the accepted case is the bound itself, 10. Under `>` it is one below the bound, so no
-- test checks that a visit of exactly 600 minutes or a deposit of exactly 1000 is accepted, the
-- value that tells `>` from `>=`. For the decimal `amount`, 999 is not the value next to the
-- bound either. The nearest work item is OQ56's boundary synthesis, "the two bounds themselves
-- under `between`", which does not name `>`.
act Member { name: text }

act Visit {
    member: one Member
    minutes: integer
}

never (Visit where minutes > 600)

transient act MakeDeposit {
    member: one Member
    amount: decimal
}

shape Deposit {
    member: one Member
    amount: decimal
}

rule RecordDeposit when MakeDeposit {
    Deposit from { member: member, amount: amount }
}

never (MakeDeposit where amount > 1000)

never (MakeDeposit where amount < 10)
